From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 14:46:36 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm: apple: t8132: Send nothing to a power-gated DCP
 from the colour paths

After a blank, the J604's DCP is powered down when power_gate_ms runs
out. Its CPU is stopped and its DARTs and domains are off until the
next frame powers it up. The CTM work, the True Tone store
(panel_adaptation), the BLM property work and the adaptive-sync update
check only powered_off (system sleep), not gated. A True Tone ramp
from userspace while the display is off and gated therefore sends A423
set_matrix to the stopped CPU:

  RTKit: Endpoint 0x37 is not running, cannot send message
  Retained DCP session quarantined: -22
  DCP A423 failed: -22; retained session

That failed session leaves the panel dark until a reboot. It shows
after a deep sleep, because the ambient white point changes across a
lid close and the True Tone service ramps while the panel is still off.
It also happens with no sleep at all: writing the current matrix back
to panel_adaptation 20 s after a blank reproduces it.

While gated, keep the matrix and the BLM properties pending.
iomfb_m4_power_ungate() marks both to be resent, and the first frame's
swap queues them (iomfb_m4_idle_cache_kick()), so they reach the
firmware right after the power-up, as after any other blank.

Fixes: 82ed2d32df09 ("drm/apple: m4: power the internal DCP and its domains down while blanked")
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/apple/iomfb_m4.c | 14 ++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/iomfb_m4.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/iomfb_m4.c
index 0724d287d4..a6b2497983 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/iomfb_m4.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/iomfb_m4.c
@@ -4948,7 +4948,7 @@ void iomfb_m4_atomic_vrr(struct apple_dcp *owner, bool vrr_enabled)
 	if ((dcp->vrr_min_sent || (adaptive && hz) || media ||
 	     READ_ONCE(panel_hold_fixed)) &&
 	    (min != dcp->vrr_min_sent || media != dcp->vrr_media_sent) &&
-	    dcp->runtime && !dcp->powered_off &&
+	    dcp->runtime && !dcp->powered_off && !dcp->gated &&
 	    !dcp_m4_set_adaptive_sync(dcp, min, media)) {
 		dcp->vrr_min_sent = min;
 		dcp->vrr_media_sent = media;
@@ -5601,8 +5601,13 @@ static void iomfb_m4_ctm_work(struct work_struct *work)
 
 	mutex_lock(&dcp->lock);
 	/* An RPC failure has already failed the session. */
+	/*
+	 * Not while powered down after a blank (iomfb_m4_power_gate()): the matrix
+	 * stays pending and goes out after the next frame's power-up (the swap's
+	 * iomfb_m4_idle_cache_kick()). An A423 to the stopped CPU fails the session.
+	 */
 	if (READ_ONCE(dcp->owner->quiescing) || !dcp->runtime || dcp->external ||
-	    dcp->powered_off || !dcp->ctm_pending)
+	    dcp->powered_off || dcp->gated || !dcp->ctm_pending)
 		goto out;
 	dcp->ctm_pending = false;
 	memcpy(req.matrix, dcp->ctm_fw, sizeof(req.matrix));
@@ -5722,7 +5727,7 @@ static ssize_t panel_adaptation_store(struct device *dev,
 	for (i = 0; i < 9; i++)
 		dcp->ctm_adapt[i] = iomfb_m4_ctm_clamp(m[i]);
 	iomfb_m4_ctm_compose(dcp);
-	if (dcp->ctm_pending && dcp->runtime && !dcp->powered_off &&
+	if (dcp->ctm_pending && dcp->runtime && !dcp->powered_off && !dcp->gated &&
 	    !READ_ONCE(dcp->owner->quiescing))
 		mod_delayed_work(dcp->runtime->wq, &dcp->ctm_work, 0);
 	mutex_unlock(&dcp->lock);
@@ -5750,8 +5755,9 @@ static void iomfb_m4_blm_work(struct work_struct *work)
 	gen = atomic_read(&blm_ah_gen);
 	mode = READ_ONCE(blm_ah_mode);
 	/* An RPC failure has already failed the session. */
+	/* Powered down after a blank: the power-up sets blm_gen = -1 and resends. */
 	if (READ_ONCE(dcp->owner->quiescing) || !dcp->runtime || dcp->external ||
-	    dcp->powered_off || gen == dcp->blm_gen)
+	    dcp->powered_off || dcp->gated || gen == dcp->blm_gen)
 		goto out;
 	dcp->blm_gen = gen;
 	mutex_lock(&blm_props_lock);
-- 
2.43.0

